1. API Overview

The suprakernel exposes a modular API with six primary subsystems:

Manifold Kernel

Topological Filtration Engine

Void Lattice Engine

ODE Convergence Engine

Homomorphic Encryption Kernel

Ledger Commit System

All modules communicate through a shared state vector:

StateVector S = {
    rho: float[],
    phi: float[],
    amplitude: float[],
    topology: object,
    lattice: object,
    metadata: object
}

2. MODULE: Manifold Kernel API

Endpoint: /manifold/evolve

Description:Evolves gravitational potential, amplitude field, and energy density.

Request:

POST /manifold/evolve
{
    "rho": [...],
    "phi": [...],
    "amplitude": [...],
    "dt": 0.001
}

Response:

{
    "phi_next": [...],
    "amplitude_next": [...],
    "gradients": {
        "rho_grad": [...],
        "phi_grad": [...],
        "amp_grad": [...]
    }
}

Notes:

Uses Hamiltonian evolution

Includes post‑Newtonian corrections

Outputs gradients for AMR refinement

3. MODULE: Topological Filtration API

Endpoint: /topology/filtration

Description:Computes persistent homology and Betti numbers.

Request:

POST /topology/filtration
{
    "density_field": [...],
    "resolution": "high"
}

Response:

{
    "betti": {
        "betti0": [...],
        "betti1": [...],
        "betti2": [...]
    },
    "birth_death": [...],
    "signature": "T_s_epoch_12"
}

Notes:

Produces topological signature

Supports multi‑resolution filtration

4. MODULE: Void Lattice Engine API

Endpoint: /lattice/evolve

Description:Evolves void lattice length under thermodynamic feedback.

Request:

POST /lattice/evolve
{
    "amplitude": [...],
    "rho": [...],
    "state": {...},
    "dt": 0.001
}

Response:

{
    "lattice_length": 0.442,
    "growth_curve": [...],
    "entropy": 1.92
